# API and design conventions

- Version public HTTP APIs under `/api/v1/...`
- Idempotent GETs; mutating operations documented and validated
- Pagination/sorting for list endpoints; default page size capped
- OpenAPI annotations kept in sync with actual endpoints

## Ticket soft-delete

- Ticket removal is **soft-delete only** via `deletedAt` (`Ticket.softDelete()`, `TicketService.softDelete`).
- Do not add hard `DELETE FROM` / `deleteById` removal of ticket rows unless explicitly requested.
- Reads/lists/get-by-id must ignore soft-deleted tickets (`deletedAt IS NULL` / active queries).
- API `DELETE /api/v1/tickets/{id}` means soft-delete; subsequent GET returns 404.

## Schema migrations (Flyway only)

- Schema changes **only** via new Flyway versioned migrations in `src/main/resources/db/migration/`.
- Keep `spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate` (non-mutating); no Hibernate `update`/`create` in committed prod/local config.
- Do not add Liquibase.

## Security and safety

- Do not weaken auth, authorization, or validation unless explicitly asked.
- Validate and sanitize inputs at the boundary; trust internal layers less at edges.
- Principle of least privilege for roles/endpoints.
- No credentials in source, tests, or logs; use env/config and test fixtures with fakes.

### Auth and roles (baseline)

Roles are exactly: `AGENT`, `MANAGER`, `ADMIN` (`com.vmticket.user.entity.Role`). Do not invent roles, reintroduce `REQUESTER`, widen `@PreAuthorize`, or disable security (`app.security.enabled=false`) unless explicitly asked.

Ticket endpoint matrix (preserve unless explicitly changing auth):

- `GET` tickets — any authenticated
- `POST` tickets — `AGENT`, `MANAGER`, `ADMIN`
- `PATCH` tickets — `AGENT`, `MANAGER`, `ADMIN`
- `DELETE` tickets — `ADMIN` (soft-delete)

Category endpoint matrix (preserve unless explicitly changing auth):

- `GET` categories — any authenticated
- `POST` categories — `MANAGER`, `ADMIN`
- `PATCH` categories — `MANAGER`, `ADMIN`
- no `DELETE`; `isArchived` hides a category from the default list only

Comment and attachment endpoint matrix (preserve unless explicitly changing auth):

- View comments and download files — any authenticated user, and only for a ticket that is not soft-deleted
- Create comment — the ticket’s assigned agent, the ticket’s assigned manager, or `ADMIN`
- No comment edit or delete
- Remove attachment — the uploader, that ticket’s manager, or `ADMIN`
- Files may be added only when a ticket or a comment is created
- List and download ticket files — any authenticated user, and only for a ticket that is not soft-deleted
- Remove a ticket file — the uploader, that ticket’s manager, or `ADMIN`

User endpoint matrix (preserve unless explicitly changing auth):

- `GET` list and get-by-id — `MANAGER` or `ADMIN`
- `POST` — `MANAGER` or `ADMIN`; a manager may assign only `AGENT`; an admin may assign only `AGENT` or `MANAGER`
- `PATCH` role — `ADMIN` only, and only `AGENT` ↔ `MANAGER`
- `DELETE` — `ADMIN` only, soft-delete of an active `AGENT`
- Deleted users stay referenced by existing work and cannot be newly assigned
- Tickets and comments must not create users

Non-prod login issues an opaque token for an existing active user. Roles come from `user_roles`. Logout deletes that token. A soft-deleted user's tokens are deleted. Custom config uses `app.security.*` / `app.auth.token-ttl` via `AppSecurityProperties`. Code wins over README if they diverge.

Auth/role behavior changes require tests (unit and/or existing `@SpringBootTest` API patterns). Detailed auth/roles guidance will be expanded in a later rules pass—do not redesign auth in drive-by changes.
